      "heading": "The Four Continuity Relics of 14 Balaram Ghosh Street",
      "body": "Across eighty years, the physical continuity of the Roy household was anchored by four unchanging physical artifacts: the notched brass key to the southern terrace gate, the parijat tree planted in 1950, the 1928 Junghans pendulum wall clock wound every Sunday at eight, and the Burma teak doorframe of the ground-floor library recording sixty-seven years of family heights.",
