      "body": "We do not own a house; we are merely granted custody of its air, its light, and its shadows for the brief span of our breathing. If we inhabit it with reverence, if we oil its latches and celebrate its seasons, the timber and the brick will return the favor. They will keep our secrets, hold our measurements, and echo our footsteps long after we have returned to the dust."
